# 📁 Raw Data Documentation (`row_data`)

This directory contains the source datasets used to build the **Sales Analysis & Business Intelligence Dashboard**. The raw data originates from enterprise transactional tables containing customer, product, regional, and sales history records.

---

## 📌 Datasets Overview

| File Name | Sheet Name(s) | Total Records | Total Columns | Primary Key | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`Customers.xlsx`** | `Sheet1` | 19,119 | 6 | `CustomerID` | Demographic details and contact information of registered clients. |
| **`Products.xlsx`** | `Sheet2` | 295 | 11 | `ProductID` | Catalog of items, categories, subcategories, cost, and pricing details. |
| **`Regions.xlsx`** | `Sheet1` | 10 | 4 | `TerritoryID` | Geographical mapping of sales territories, country codes, and regions. |
| **`Sales.xlsx`** | `2011`, `2012`, `2013`, `2014` | 121,318 | 10 | Composite / Line Item | Historical transactional sales line items across 4 calendar years. |

---

## 🗺️ Data Schema & Relationships

The dataset is structured as a **Star Schema** to optimize reporting and relational data modeling in Power BI:

```text
       ┌───────────────┐
       │   Customers   │
       └───────┬───────┘
               │ (1:N)
               ▼
┌─────────────────────────────┐         ┌───────────────┐
│         Sales (Fact)        │◄──(N:1)─┤   Products    │
└──────────────┬──────────────┘         └───────────────┘
               │ (N:1)
               ▼
       ┌───────────────┐
       │    Regions    │
       └───────────────┘
📖 Data Dictionary
👥 1. Customers (Customers.xlsx)
Column Name	Data Type	Key Type	Description
CustomerID	Integer	Primary Key	Unique integer identifier for each customer
StoreID	Float / Null	Foreign Key	Store identifier if applicable
AccountNumber	String	Unique Code	Account reference number (e.g., AW00029484)
FirstName	String	Feature	Customer's first name
LastName	String	Feature	Customer's last name
Title	String	Feature	Honorific title (e.g., Mr., Ms.)
📦 2. Products (Products.xlsx)
Column Name	Data Type	Key Type	Description
ProductID	Integer	Primary Key	Unique SKU identifier
ProductName	String	Feature	Full descriptive name of the product
ProductCategoryID	Integer	ID	Numerical ID for main product category
Product Category	String	Feature	Main category (Bikes, Components, Clothing, Accessories)
Product Subcategory	String	Feature	Granular subcategory (e.g., Road Frames, Mountain Bikes)
ProductSubcategoryID	Integer	ID	Numerical ID for product subcategory
Color	String	Feature	Color variant (e.g., Black, Red, Yellow)
StandardCost	Float	Metric	Base manufacturing / acquisition cost
ListPrice	Float	Metric	Catalog retail selling price
SellStartDate	DateTime	Feature	Date when product was introduced to market
SellEndDate	DateTime / Null	Feature	End of life date (if discontinued)
🌍 3. Regions (Regions.xlsx)
Column Name	Data Type	Key Type	Description
TerritoryID	Integer	Primary Key	Numerical territory code
Region Name	String	Feature	Local region name (e.g., Northwest, United Kingdom)
CountryRegionCode	String	Feature	ISO 2-letter country code (US, GB, DE, FR, AU)
Region Group	String	Feature	Continental group (North America, Europe, Pacific)
🛒 4. Sales (Sales.xlsx)
Column Name	Data Type	Key Type	Description
OrderDate	DateTime	Dimension	Transaction date
CustomerID	Integer	Foreign Key	References Customers.CustomerID
TerritoryID	Integer	Foreign Key	References Regions.TerritoryID
SalesOrderID	Integer	Transaction ID	Sales order header identifier
CarrierTrackingNumber	String / Null	Metric	Shipment carrier tracking ID
OrderQty	Integer	Measure	Quantity of units purchased in line item
ProductID	Integer	Foreign Key	References Products.ProductID
SpecialOfferID	Integer	Feature	Applied promotion code
UnitPriceDiscount	Float	Measure	Applied discount monetary value
ModifiedDate	DateTime	System	Date record was last updated
🛠️ ETL & Data Transformation Guidelines
Table Union (Sales Sheets): Combine all 4 annual sheets (2011, 2012, 2013, 2014) in Sales.xlsx into a single consolidated FactSales table.

Data Cleaning: Handle null values in CarrierTrackingNumber (non-shipped/digital items) and SellEndDate (active catalog products).

Relationships Setup: Configure single-direction 1-to-Many (1:N) relationships running from Dimension tables (Customers, Products, Regions) to FactSales.
